From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:14:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 166/167] hjviewer: the iPhone app asks for no push or Wi-Fi
 information entitlement

Upstream's Runner.entitlements asks for aps-environment (push) and
com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info. The app uses neither: no plugin
or line of the app registers for remote notifications or reads the Wi-Fi
network (no firebase_messaging, no CNCopyCurrentNetworkInfo or
NEHotspotNetwork, no UIBackgroundModes), and HJViewer's App ID grants
neither capability, so the iOS build's signing step deleted both keys on
every build with a warning each. The file now holds an empty dict: the
app is signed with the same entitlements as before, the profile's own,
and the signing step's loop finds neither key and says nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flutter/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements b/flutter/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements
index 75e36a1..0c67376 100644
--- a/flutter/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements
+++ b/flutter/ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements
@@ -1,10 +1,5 @@
 <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
 <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
 <plist version="1.0">
-<dict>
-	<key>aps-environment</key>
-	<string>development</string>
-	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info</key>
-	<true/>
-</dict>
+<dict/>
 </plist>
